# cw-tune-on: the same CW page as cw-tune-off with the "Tuner" button pressed, so
# the CW tune widget appears (issue #122).
#
# Same route (KEY pages -> "(CW 1:2)"); the difference is scenario_settle pressing
# the page's "Tuner" button (index 2), which runs the user's path
# button_action_cb -> controls_toggle_cw_tuner -> cfg.cw_tune (src/buttons.cpp,
# src/controls.cpp). With the rig in CW and cw_tune=1, update_visibility()
# (src/cw_tune_ui.c) clears the widget's hidden flag: this capture is the fix path
# the radio takes once the parameter is on (the port ships it off, src/cfg/cfg.c).
#
# The active block is drawn by the real cw_tune_set_freq() with a synthetic 8 Hz
# tone: on the radio the tone comes from the DSP (src/cw.cpp, update_peak_freq),
# which the bank has no way to feed. scenario_settle codifies the parameter, the
# button label and the widget's visibility.

name cw-tune-on
screen cw-tune-on

theme Redshift
seed 20

frequency_hz 7030000
tx_frequency_hz 7030000
fft_width_hz 384000

mode cw
vfo A
agc auto

split false
att false
pre false
atu false
ant 1

smeter_db -73

battery_v 12.1
external_v 13.8
battery_cap 76
charging false

rxtx rx
